---
// H1–H2: one stubborn person in a room that runs a consensus-seeking rule; the same on a toy network, where a quiet
// node changes nothing and an important one flips everyone (each run waits for its own start); then clamp every node
// in turn for its dynamical importance, our result. The limitations are for the questions, not the slides.
// Data: src/data/defence/clamp.json.
import Slide from './Slide.astro';
import Seats from './Seats.astro';
import SimButton from './SimButton.astro';
import clamp from '../../data/defence/clamp.json';
---
<Slide id="ch-impact" label="The stubborn person" builds={6} class="h1" ch={10}>
  <div class="row grow h1-row">
    <div class="stack h1-view">
      <div class="h1-seats" data-b-off="1"><Seats label="The room with every hand up except one" /></div>
      <div class="h1-box" data-b="1">
        <canvas class="net" aria-label="A network of 100 people running a consensus-seeking rule, one of them clamped"></canvas>
        <SimButton class="h1-btn" />
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col h1-side">
      <h2>The stubborn person</h2>
      <p class="lede">Everyone follows a consensus-seeking rule, and the room ends with every hand up.</p>
      <p class="lede">Now one person refuses: <span class="danger">hand down, no matter what</span>. Does the room follow?</p>
      <p class="h1-state" data-state></p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="cite">A consensus-seeking rule on a scale-free network of 100 people, about eight contacts each · the same start every time</p>
  <p class="illus" data-b="1">illustration</p>
  <p slot="say">The second application uses the consensus-seeking rules that were such bad detectives. Imagine everyone in the room follows one: after a few rounds every hand is up. Now one person refuses and keeps their hand down, whatever happens. Does the room follow them?</p>
  <p slot="say">The same on a network of 100 people. With nobody stubborn, it ends with every hand up. When a quiet person at the edge is stubborn (ringed), nobody else follows. When an important person is stubborn, the whole network flips to every hand down. Holding one node fixed like this is called clamping, or pinning: it is an intervention, not just an observation.</p>
</Slide>

<Slide label="Clamp everyone, one at a time" builds={2} class="h2" ch={10}>
  <h2>Clamp everyone, one at a time</h2>
  <div class="row grow h2-row">
    <canvas class="net" aria-label="The network with every person coloured by how much the room follows them when they are stubborn"></canvas>
    <div class="col h2-side">
      <p><b>Importance</b>: how much of the room ends up with a hand down, on average, when this person is stubborn.</p>
      <canvas class="hist" data-b-off="1" aria-label="How many people have each importance"></canvas>
      <canvas class="scatter" data-b="1" aria-label="Importance against the number of contacts"></canvas>
      <p class="result" data-b="2"><b>Our result</b> An importance found by simulation alone. It goes with how central a person is, but no single measure of centrality explains it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="cite">Chapter 10, work in progress · {clamp.summary.starts} starts that reach consensus, each person stubborn in each</p>
  <p class="illus">illustration</p>
  <p slot="say">Now make everyone stubborn in turn, one at a time, and record how much of the room ends up with a hand down: that is each person’s dynamical importance. On this network most people change almost nothing, and a few flip the room most of the time.</p>
  <p slot="say">Against the number of contacts, importance is clearly related to position, but not one-to-one. In the thesis, across families of networks, it correlates with the usual measures of centrality but reduces to none of them; in one family, a node whose neighbours are hubs even matters less. What makes the score attractive is that it needs no measure of centrality at all, only the ability to simulate, and we rarely know the rule that real people or cells follow. This part of the thesis is unpublished and still in progress; its limitations are in the thesis and gladly discussed afterwards.</p>
</Slide>

<style>
  .h1-row { gap: calc(60 * var(--u)); align-items: center; }
  .h1-view { width: calc(900 * var(--u)); height: calc(900 * var(--u)); flex: none; place-items: center; }
  .h1-seats :global(.seats) { height: calc(880 * var(--u)); width: auto; }
  .h1-box { position: relative; }
  .h1-box canvas { display: block; width: calc(840 * var(--u)); height: calc(840 * var(--u)); }
  .h1-box :global(.h1-btn) { right: calc(10 * var(--u)); bottom: calc(10 * var(--u)); }
  .h1-side { gap: calc(34 * var(--u)); }
  .h1-state { font-size: calc(34 * var(--u)); min-height: 3em; }

  .h2-row { gap: calc(50 * var(--u)); align-items: flex-start; }
  .h2-row > canvas.net { width: calc(740 * var(--u)); height: calc(740 * var(--u)); flex: none; }
  .h2-side { gap: calc(24 * var(--u)); flex: 1; }
  .hist, .scatter { width: calc(820 * var(--u)); height: calc(420 * var(--u)); }
  .scatter { margin-top: calc(-444 * var(--u)); }
  :global(.h2) .result { font-size: calc(34 * var(--u)); }
</style>

<script>
  import { slide, sim, type How } from '../../scripts/defence/deck';
  import { stage, onSize, ticker } from '../../scripts/defence/stage';
  import { axes, dot, label, px, py, type Plot } from '../../scripts/defence/plot';
  import { type Rule, density } from '../../scripts/llna';
  import { stepClamped } from '../../scripts/consensus';
  import { build } from '../../scripts/net';
  import { parse, mix, css } from '../../scripts/palette';
  import clamp from '../../data/defence/clamp.json';

  const RULE: Rule = { r: 9, B: 464, S: 488 };
  const n = clamp.deg.length, net = build('ba', n, clamp.edges as [number, number][]);
  const X = (i: number, b: { x: number; w: number }) => b.x + clamp.xy[2 * i] * b.w, Y = (i: number, b: { y: number; h: number }) => b.y + clamp.xy[2 * i + 1] * b.h;
  const radius = (i: number) => 7 + 1.6 * Math.sqrt(clamp.deg[i]);

  /** The network: faint links, then the people, filled when their hand is up. */
  function drawNet(st: NonNullable<ReturnType<typeof stage>>, state: (i: number) => string, ring: (i: number) => string | null) {
    const { ctx, t } = st, b = { x: 30, y: 30, w: st.w - 60, h: st.h - 60 };
    ctx.strokeStyle = t.line; ctx.lineWidth = 1.5; ctx.beginPath();
    for (const [i, j] of clamp.edges) { ctx.moveTo(X(i, b), Y(i, b)); ctx.lineTo(X(j, b), Y(j, b)); }
    ctx.stroke();
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(X(i, b), Y(i, b), radius(i), 0, 2 * Math.PI);
      ctx.fillStyle = state(i); ctx.fill(); ctx.lineWidth = 2; ctx.strokeStyle = t.muted; ctx.stroke();
      const r = ring(i);
      if (r) { ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(X(i, b), Y(i, b), radius(i) + 10, 0, 2 * Math.PI); ctx.lineWidth = 6; ctx.strokeStyle = r; ctx.stroke(); }
    }
  }

  // ── H1: the room, then the network: nobody stubborn (shown at build 1, run at 2), a quiet one (3, 4), an important
  // one (5, 6) ──
  for (const s of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.slide.h1')) {
    const c = s.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('canvas.net')!, out = s.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-state]')!;
    const svg = s.querySelector<SVGSVGElement>('svg.seats')!, seats = Array.from(svg.querySelectorAll<SVGUseElement>('use.seat'));
    for (const u of seats) { u.setAttribute('href', '#hand-up'); u.classList.replace('down', 'up'); }
    seats[3 * 8 + 5].setAttribute('href', '#hand-down'); seats[3 * 8 + 5].classList.replace('up', 'stubborn');
    const start = Uint8Array.from(clamp.demo.bits, (ch) => +ch), { hi, lo } = clamp.demo;
    let who = -1, a = start.slice(), b = new Uint8Array(n), tick = 0, cl = new Int8Array(n).fill(-1), done = false, at = 0;
    function reset(k: number) {
      who = k; cl.fill(-1); a = start.slice(); tick = 0; done = false;
      if (k >= 0) { cl[k] = 0; a[k] = 0; }
    }
    function paint() {
      const st = stage(c); if (!st) return;
      const { t } = st;
      drawNet(st, (i) => (a[i] ? t.ink : t.panel), (i) => (i === who ? t.danger : null));
      const up = Math.round(density(a) * n);
      if (at === 0) { out.textContent = ''; return; }
      out.innerHTML = `round ${tick} · ${up} of ${n} hands up` + (done ? (up <= 0 ? '<br><b class="danger">the whole room followed</b>' : who >= 0 ? '<br>nobody else followed' : '<br>consensus: every hand up') : '');
    }
    const advance = () => {
      stepClamped(a, net, RULE, cl, b); [a, b] = [b, a]; tick++;
      const r = density(a);
      if (tick >= 40 || r === 0 || r === 1 || (who >= 0 && r >= 1 - 1.5 / n && tick > 12)) { done = true; return true; }
      return false;
    };
    const run = ticker(s, 3, advance, paint);
    const nodeAt = (k: number) => (k >= 5 ? hi : k >= 3 ? lo : -1);
    sim(s.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-simbtn]')!, [2, 4, 6], { reset() { run.play(false); reset(nodeAt(at)); paint(); }, play() { run.play(true); } });
    slide(s, {
      // going back to a run shows how it ended; the button's waiting builds reset it
      set(k: number, how: How) {
        at = k;
        if (nodeAt(k) !== who || how !== 'next') { run.play(false); reset(nodeAt(k)); if (how === 'prev' && k % 2 === 0 && k > 0) while (!advance()); }
        paint();
      },
      enter() { reset(-1); },
      leave() { run.play(false); },
    });
    onSize(c, paint);
  }

  // ── H2: everyone's importance on the network, its spread, and against the number of contacts ──
  for (const s of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.slide.h2')) {
    const [nc, hc, sc] = Array.from(s.querySelectorAll<HTMLCanvasElement>('canvas'));
    const eta = clamp.eta, top = Math.max(...eta);
    onSize(nc, () => {
      const st = stage(nc); if (!st) return;
      const lo = parse(st.t.panel), hiC = parse(st.t.accent);
      drawNet(st, (i) => css(mix(lo, hiC, eta[i] / top)), () => null);
      label(st, 'darker: the room follows this person more', 30, st.h - 8, { size: 26, color: st.t.muted });
    });
    onSize(hc, () => {
      const st = stage(hc); if (!st) return;
      const bins = 16, counts = new Array(bins).fill(0);
      for (const v of eta) counts[Math.min(bins - 1, Math.floor((v / 0.8) * bins))]++;
      const p: Plot = { x: 150, y: 20, w: st.w - 180, h: st.h - 130, x0: 0, x1: 0.8, y0: 0, y1: Math.max(...counts) * 1.1 };
      axes(st, p, { xticks: [[0, 'none'], [0.8, 'high']], yticks: [[0, '0'], [Math.max(...counts), String(Math.max(...counts))]], xname: 'importance', yname: 'people' });
      counts.forEach((k, b) => { st.ctx.fillStyle = st.t.accent; st.ctx.fillRect(px(p, (b * 0.8) / bins) + 2, py(p, k), (p.w / bins) - 4, py(p, 0) - py(p, k)); });
    });
    onSize(sc, () => {
      const st = stage(sc); if (!st) return;
      const kmax = Math.max(...clamp.deg), p: Plot = { x: 150, y: 20, w: st.w - 180, h: st.h - 130, x0: 0, x1: kmax + 2, y0: 0, y1: 0.85 };
      axes(st, p, { xticks: [[4, '4'], [10, '10'], [20, '20'], [30, '30']].filter(([v]) => (v as number) <= kmax + 2) as [number, string][], yticks: [[0, 'none'], [0.8, 'high']], xname: 'contacts', yname: 'importance' });
      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) dot(st, px(p, clamp.deg[i]), py(p, eta[i]), 8, st.t.accent);
    });
  }
</script>
